{"title":"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c5c96b5fc71513978687cb5076d21f4536d05f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> is an integral multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b56d32444d8efd65eb0cb6c01f8ac72c32587e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are real numbers. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/8429d190ea4b16c02d5d552f9a64ed70bcd681a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\sin(A)+y\\sin(B)+z\\sin(C)=x^2\\sin(2A)+y^2\\sin(2B)+z^2\\sin(2C)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"579\" height=\"21\" />, show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70ea7d6026ca0cdaca5f96c2b5760606fa083397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n\\sin(nA)+y^n \\sin(nB) +z^n \\sin(nC)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"327\" height=\"18\" /> for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/38715c3b00059bfa80905cf14748ab22d6c28fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=xe^{iA}$\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e533bf3f9197c8a6df48ab6b82ce90e7cf79341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=ye^{iB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/8887ed8527a379bfe41a6a6df42fbc12205f123a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=ze^{iC}$\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" /> be numbers in the complex plane. \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd6c1269d2e83c7baf547059b6da4e31abad860a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B+C=k\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a800ffb3597a2c9b49f7beb0329afbf5b11a156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=xyz(e^{ik\\pi})=\\pm xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"20\" /> which is real. Also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b53f635ffa4a5597c0d246df371f34a95131cb24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\sin(A), y\\sin(B), z\\sin(C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> are the imaginary parts of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076ec4373cfdf376c7947aeeedbeb30552debe57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\sin(2A), y^2\\sin(2B), z^2\\sin(2C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"254\" height=\"19\" /> are the imaginary parts of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098ee923e05adbc0f239d8864e5af3b00dba169c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2, b^2, c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> by de Moivre's Theorem. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac816c290967e49b43b79af7c7fbb65dc613f4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> are real because their imaginary parts sum to zero.\n</p><p>Finally, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b8715fd758d42e65ea17d35b7ece966e2a9e26b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\left((a+b+c)^2-(a^2+b^2+c^2)\\right)=ab+bc+ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"371\" height=\"37\" /> is real as well.\n</p><p>It suffices to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69e4449279dc225e1201318fab463cd77760640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n=a^n+b^n+c^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" /> is real for all positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, which can be shown by induction.\n</p><p>Newton Sums gives the following relationship between sums of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d7ec7a8a390bcfc3db851e0c934fffb47ec5b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k=a^k+b^k+c^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb07df2853b8a0fe916a95b664d07e9e0407ca5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_k-S_1P_{k-1}+S_2P_{k-2}-S_3P_{k-3}=0\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"15\" />\nWhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38cc24f087235e5056ccbacba8fb047124bbbcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1=a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94e8bd4614828f2771d4a3458ce8664b34d9090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2=ab+bc+ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffe151b8363bb8d7f95c9e5b99042424aca0e19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_3=abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />. It is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a699836e1a170226a05ebdde8bfd4c39f009b04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0, P_1, P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> are real. Note that if  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71ed47e178f1e683db8272981f233e7b8ca28015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{k-1}, P_{k-2}, P_{k-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" /> are real, then clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is real because all other parts of the above equation are real, completing the induction.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO\" title=\"1980 USAMO\">1980 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1980\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173417\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 187/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5320/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.615      1 -total\n 54.44%    6.868      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 43.03%    5.428      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11414:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173417 and revision id 85582. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}